              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 3 buses carried 162 students and teacher. All the buses are full so capacity of one bus "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 6 2 } { 3 } = 5 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let there be x number of buses for 204 student. Now, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 : 1 6 2 : x"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " : 204 So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = { \\frac { 3 4 } { 9 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " We need 4 buses. Number of seats in 4 buses "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 \\times 54 = 216"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Total number of students and teachers = 204 So, 216 – 204 = 12 seats will remain vacant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.302,
            0.848,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The area of Delhi is 1,484 sq. km and the area of Mumbai is 550 sq. km. The population of Delhi is approximately 30 million and that of Mumbai is 20 million people. Which city is more crowded? Why do you say so?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.383,
            0.847,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Calculate the number of persons in 1sq. km of both Delhi and Mumbai Number of persons per sq. km in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Dellhi}=\\frac{3000000}{1484} \\approx 20216"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Number of persons per sq. km in Mumba "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2000000}{550} \\approx 36,364"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Since, Number of persons per sq. km in Mumbai is more than in Delhi so, Mumbai is more crowded."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.539,
            0.847,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A crane of height 155 cm has its neck and the rest of its body in the ratio 4 : 6. For your height, if your neck and the rest of the body also had this ratio, how tall would your neck be?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.601,
            0.692,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The ratio of the neck and rest body of crane is 4:6. Measure your height. Neck height "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= \\frac{4}{10} \\times"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " your height"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.69,
            0.848,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Let us try an ancient problem from Līlāvatī. At that time weights were measured in a unit named palas and niskas was a unit of money. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\underset{\\cdot \\cdot }{\\overset{\\cdot \\cdot \\cdot }{\\mathrm{Tr}}} 2 \\frac{1}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " palas of saffron costs "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 7 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " niskas, O expert businessman! tell me quickly what quantity of saffron can be bought for 9 niskas?”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.78,
            0.306,
            0.8
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 52.5 palas"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.811,
            0.732,
            0.833
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence 52.5 palas of saffron can be bought for 9 niskas"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.841,
            0.848,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": [
